    <string name="help_title_pantry_list">My Pantry</string>
    <string name="help_body_pantry_list">This is everything you currently have in your pantry.\n\n• Tap an item to edit it.\n• Swipe left on an item to delete it.\n• Use the search bar to quickly find an ingredient.\n• Tap the + button to add a new ingredient.\n\nYou can change an ingredient\'s quantity, unit, food icon, or expiry date.</string>

    <string name="help_title_suggested_recipes">Suggested Recipes</string>
    <string name="help_body_suggested_recipes">This screen checks the ingredients in your pantry against the available recipes.\n\n• Ready to make — you have all the required ingredients in the required amounts.\n• Almost there — you are missing only one ingredient or do not have enough of one ingredient.\n• Tap a recipe to see its ingredients and details.\n\nHaving an ingredient is not always enough. For example, if a recipe needs 60 g of cheese but you only have 20 g, you do not have enough to make the recipe.</string>

    <string name="help_title_recipe_detail">Recipe Detail</string>
    <string name="help_body_recipe_detail">The badge at the top shows whether you can make this recipe with what you currently have.\n\nFor each ingredient:\n\n• ✓ means you have enough.\n• ✗ means you are missing it or do not have enough.\n\nThese are the same checks used to decide whether the recipe appears under Ready to make or Almost there.</string>

    <string name="help_title_add_edit_ingredient">Add / Edit Ingredient</string>
    <string name="help_body_add_edit_ingredient">Name, quantity, and unit are required. Everything else is optional.\n\n• The food icon updates automatically as you type the ingredient name.\n• Tap the icon if you want to choose a different one.\n• An expiry date is optional.\n\nAdding an expiry date allows the ingredient to be shown as expiring soon or expired on your Pantry screen.</string>
